                  "typeName": "processMethodsDescription",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "Volumetric oxygen mass transfer coefficients (kLa) were determined using the dynamic gassing-out method. Dissolved oxygen data were processed by fitting the linearized form ln(C* - C) versus time within the 20-80% saturation range. Mechanical power input was calculated from measured torque and rotational speed. Data processing, filtering, and visualization were performed using Python, with minor supplementary analysis conducted in MATLAB."
                },
